# A missing build asset must 404, not fall through to the SPA shell.
#
# This file used to be the catch-all alone. Because the host answers an unmatched path with
# index.html at status 200, a request for a hashed chunk that no longer exists — /assets/Landing-
# DMENHW6G.js after a deploy replaced it — came back as HTML with `Content-Type: text/html`, and the
# browser refused it with:
#
#   Failed to load module script: Expected a JavaScript-or-Wasm module script but the server
#   responded with a MIME type of "text/html"
#
# Every lazy route died at once — Landing, AppShell, Dashboard, Profile, and each icon chunk — so
# the page rendered blank with no clue pointing at the deploy. A 404 says the true thing instead,
# and is what the runtime recovery in main.jsx keys off.
#
# Existing files still win: the host serves a real static file before consulting these rules, so
# this only ever catches assets that are genuinely gone.
/assets/*  /assets/:splat  404

# Everything else is a client-side route.
/*  /index.html  200
